ial chows.\n\nB6 is in hand, but you have no B4/B7/B5 to make chow, and B6-B7-B8 not possible (B7 unshown 2, but risky).\n\nMoreover, previous player has B9 pung, next player has B8 pung, so high-level B tiles are dangerous.\n\nB6 might be safe.\n\nBut B2 is safer to discard as completely isolated.\n\nScoring potential:\n\n- If you go for Full Flush (24 points), need all suited tiles same suit. Currently have B2 \u2014 must discard.\n\n- All Chows (2 points) possible if you form four chows.\n\n- Pure Double Chow: T5-T6-T7 and T6-T7-T8 both involve T6-T7, but not identical.\n\n- Short Straight: T5-T6-T7 and T6-T7-T8 overlap.\n\nBut best is to aim for Full Flush + Pure Straight or similar.\n\nPure Straight requires T1-3, T4-6, T7-9.\n\nYou have T4 kong (counts as T4-T6 if we consider, but no \u2014 T4 is fixed.\n\nT4 is part of T4-T5-T6.\n\nYou have T5, T6, so T4-T5-T6 is covered.\n\nT7-T8-T9 missing T9.\n\nT1-T2-T3 missing.\n\nHard to complete.\n\nBut you have T5,T6,T7,T8 \u2014 can form T5-T6-T7 and T6-T7-T8 \u2014 that's Mixed Shifted Chows? No, same suit.\n\nPure Shifted Chows: three successive chows in same suit with interval 1 or 2.\n\nHere, T5-T6-T7 and T6-T7-T8 \u2014 shifted by 1, but only two such chows.\n\nNeed three for the pattern.\n\nAlternatively, wait for T9 to make T7-T8-T9.\n\nOr T4-T5-T6 (already have T4,T5,T6), T5-T6-T7, T6-T7-T8, T7-T8-T9 \u2014 overlapping.\n\nBut patterns like Pure Straight require non-overlapping.\n\nBest bet: Full Flush (24 points) + All Chows (2 points) + maybe others.\n\nCurrently, you have:\n- Meld 1: T4\u00d74 (kong) \u2014 pung/kong\n- Meld 2: [B5,B6,B7] \u2014 chow\n- Hand: T5,T6,T7,T7,T8,B2,B6\n\nAfter discarding B2, you have all Bamboos.\n\nThen aim to form chows with T5-T6-T7, T6-T7-T8, etc.\n\nYou might draw T7, T8, T9, T3, etc.\n\nT7 is common, but opponents may avoid.\n\nUnshown T7: 2 \u2014 so possible.\n\nBut safer to discard B2 to commit to flush.\n\nAmong other options, playing B6 is also possible, but you have